{"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"4866241e15c18bdbd717865c504b9facdcaf1ae0","body":"[hermit2, degraded-unresolved, gpt-6-astra, devbig014, role=impl]\n\nTask: kvm-lane-to-full-determinism-and-parity\n\n## Plain Language Summary\n\nFollowing `/proc/self/fd/N` could return different object metadata from `fstat(N)`, and opening an owned `/proc/self/fdinfo/N` returned `EACCES`. Use the real guest-owned object consistently and serve fdinfo with Linux read, seek, descriptor-reuse and lifetime behavior.\n\n## Project Impact\n\nKeep the repair within six private KVM backend files. Preserve captured/synthetic identities and supervisor procfs isolation. Capture the actual backend mount snapshot for existing Tool sanitization. Downstream Hermit mount-provenance integration and rebuilt-CLI checks for https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3047 remain pending; these native results do not establish that assertion or complete backend parity.\n\n## Determinism\n\nOwned host metadata remains input to existing Tool normalization. Ordinary descriptor routes now use the same object identity as direct fstat. No scheduler ordering, clocks, INFO records, comparator or selection requirements change. A changing host filesystem remains outside the backend's determinism guarantee.\n\n## Linux Semantics\n\nFdinfo retains the pathname-selected task and original descriptor-table lifetime, observes current offset/status and per-descriptor `O_CLOEXEC`, and shares sequence state across aliases. It preserves pread/file-offset separation, partial-copy faults, rewind and failed-seek behavior. Invalid original user ranges and unsupported `O_DIRECT` changes fail before mutating sequence or flags. Private/captured fdinfo targets and unsupported transfer/vector routes remain explicit refusals; mount IDs and object-specific fields are not fabricated.\n\n## Validation\n\nAll 37 selected native executor, memory and mount controls passed, including alias/reuse comparisons against native fstat and the existing executable-link replacement/deletion test (0.229 CPU / 1.017 wall seconds). Pinned-toolchain Clippy passed with `--locked --offline -p reverie-kvm --lib --tests -- -D warnings` (40.808 CPU / 22.047 wall seconds); formatting and diff checks passed. All source/tool/executable bindings matched and all four services were inactive and empty afterward.\n\nThe earlier missing-argument compile failure and 35-pass/1-fail private-versus-visible identity assertion result remain preserved. The corrected test retains private alias/nonreuse assertions and strengthens native/guest/followed-stat/readlink comparisons. External production review is pending; external approval of the test-only correction is scoped to that delta. No Hermit or KVM guest run is included in this validation.\n\n## KVM Relationship to gVisor\n\nKeep the existing separation documented in `reverie-kvm/README.md`: KVM carries the Linux register frame, the executor owns descriptor/ABI handling, and subscribed calls pass through Tool policy. Linux proc/sequence-file semantics guide this implementation. It copies no gVisor code and adds no Sentry VFS or virtual mount namespace.\n","headRefName":"codex/kvm-proc-fd-identity-20260917","headRefOid":"696f0476aa46cf29e31b947a89379d80b4542ce3","isDraft":true,"labels":[],"mergeStateStatus":"CLEAN","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","number":565,"reviewDecision":"","state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[],"title":"Preserve KVM proc descriptor metadata and fdinfo semantics","url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/reverie/pull/565"}
